(7700631, 1263870, 97435, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the encouraging comments, very happy to see so many reactions!<br/> <br/>==================<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PennyStreet:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice in b/w. And so resourceful. I''m always glad when it rains so the car gets washed on the outside. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>The black SUV actually pulled up to the hydrant and was going back and forth washing the side of the car :)<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jomari:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice environmental portrait. I love the way the spray catches the light. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thank you! I wish I would''ve pulled up the photo on my computer to light up the water a little bit more though. Next time.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tnun:</b></div><hr/><i> oddly fetching. this is usually the job of the babushka. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>She''s probably watching from a window, somewhere...<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I''m honored, thank you!<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PennyStreet:</b></div><hr/><i> (... and it figures that the resourcefulness would belong to a New Yorker!) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>New Yorker at the moment, yes :)</td>', 'Thanks for all the encouraging comments, very happy to see so many reactions! ================== Originally posted by PennyStreet: Nice in b/w. And so resourceful. I''m always glad when it rains so the car gets washed on the outside.  The black SUV actually pulled up to the hydrant and was going back and forth washing the side of the car :) Originally posted by jomari: Nice environmental portrait. I love the way the spray catches the light.  Thank you! I wish I would''ve pulled up the photo on my computer to light up the water a little bit more though. Next time. Originally posted by tnun: oddly fetching. this is usually the job of the babushka.  She''s probably watching from a window, somewhere... Originally posted by posthumous: I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery  I''m honored, thank you! Originally posted by PennyStreet: (... and it figures that the resourcefulness would belong to a New Yorker!)  New Yorker at the moment, yes :)', '2021-09-07 13:48:38.000000', NULL, 0),
